@page "/"

<PageTitle>OneVision.UI</PageTitle>

<div class="ov-home-hero">
    <div>
        <div class="ov-home-kicker">OneVision design system</div>
        <h1 class="ov-gallery-page-title">Build screens from agreed controls and behaviours</h1>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="ov-gallery-page-intro">
            Start with what you are trying to build, find the closest component or pattern, exercise its states, then copy the stable UI reference or full design contract into the app specification.
        </MudText>
    </div>
    <div class="ov-home-stats"><div><strong>@ComponentCatalog.Components.Count</strong><span>components</span></div><div><strong>@PatternCatalog.Patterns.Count</strong><span>patterns</span></div></div>
</div>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-home-example" Elevation="0">
        <div>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">OVP-000 · OneVision Application Foundation</MudText>
            <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">Every OneVision application adopts the versioned root UI contract before screen-by-screen component or pattern migration.</MudText>
        </div>
        <OVButton Href="foundation">Open foundation contract</OVButton>
    </MudPaper>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <div class="ov-section-heading-row"><div><MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Start with the job</MudText><MudText Typo="Typo.body2">You do not need to know the library name first.</MudText></div></div>
    <div class="ov-start-grid">
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="components"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">⌨</span><strong>Capture or select data</strong><small>Text fields, selects, multi-selects, dates, toggles and structured field trees.</small></a>
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="patterns/list-page"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">≡</span><strong>Show or manage a list</strong><small>Search, contextual filters, compact grid, row actions and top-right pagination.</small></a>
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="patterns/edit-overlay"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">✎</span><strong>Create or edit something</strong><small>Editor, validation, dirty state, save/cancel and conditional sections.</small></a>
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="patterns/picker-overlay"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">✓</span><strong>Find and choose something</strong><small>Search, filters, selectable results and selection summary.</small></a>
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="patterns/tree-workspace"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">⌘</span><strong>Work with hierarchy</strong><small>Trees, hierarchy pickers, builders and nested structured data.</small></a>
        <a class="ov-start-card" href="patterns/run-overlay"><span class="ov-start-card__icon">▶</span><strong>Run or monitor a process</strong><small>Options, progress, result, activity and health states.</small></a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <div class="ov-section-heading-row"><div><MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Working method</MudText><MudText Typo="Typo.body2">A lightweight workflow for app design and build conversations.</MudText></div></div>
    <div class="ov-workflow-steps">
        <div><span>1</span><strong>Find</strong><small>Search by purpose, behaviour, state or reference.</small></div>
        <div><span>2</span><strong>Exercise</strong><small>Click through the live states and conditional behaviour.</small></div>
        <div><span>3</span><strong>Reference</strong><small>Copy the stable <code>OVC-...</code> or <code>OVP-...</code> identifier.</small></div>
        <div><span>4</span><strong>Specify only the difference</strong><small>Describe the domain rule the app adds; do not restate the standard UI behaviour.</small></div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <MudPaper Class="ov-home-example" Elevation="0">
        <div><MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Behaviour can be part of the UI contract</MudText><MudText Typo="Typo.body2">For example, incoming JSON fields can use the Structured Field Tree rather than a flattened field list.</MudText></div>
        <pre class="ov-code">Use OVC-STRUCTURED-FIELD-TREE.
SelectionMode = LeafOnly.
Preserve object / array hierarchy.
Selecting a leaf returns its complete JSON path.</pre>
        <OVButton Href="components/structured-field-tree">Open Structured Field Tree</OVButton>
    </MudPaper>
</section>

<section class="ov-home-section">
    <div class="ov-home-two-column">
        <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0"><MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Components</MudText><MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-4">Reusable controls with states, behaviour contracts and stable references.</MudText><MudLink Href="components">Browse all @ComponentCatalog.Components.Count components</MudLink></MudPaper>
        <MudPaper Class="ov-library-card" Elevation="0"><MudText Typo="Typo.h6">Patterns</MudText><MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-4">Reusable workflows and workspaces composed from components.</MudText><MudLink Href="patterns">Browse all @PatternCatalog.Patterns.Count patterns</MudLink></MudPaper>
    </div>
</section>
